    {
      "id": "SET-B050",
      "tag": "h3",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "2.3.5 Tempo & MIDI"
    },
    {
      "id": "SET-B051",
      "tag": "p",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "The Tempo & MIDI Settings are used to help Live recognize external devices for multiple purposes:"
    },
    {
      "id": "SET-B052",
      "tag": "li",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "Syncing the program with external devices via Tempo Follower or MIDI. Please see the Synchronizing via Tempo Follower and Synchronizing via MIDI sections for more details."
    },
    {
      "id": "SET-B053",
      "tag": "li",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "Resyncing external hardware to Live’s MIDI clock, which can be useful when synced hardware drifts out of time with the Live Set during playback. More information can be found in the Sync section of the Routing and I/O chapter."
    },
    {
      "id": "SET-B054",
      "tag": "li",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "Playing MIDI notes. To learn how to route an external device into Live for MIDI input, or how to send MIDI to an external device, please see the Routing and I/O chapter."
    },
    {
      "id": "SET-B055",
      "tag": "li",
      "anchor": "tempo--midi",
      "html_line": 416,
      "text": "Controlling parts of the interface remotely. This subject is covered in detail in the MIDI and Key Remote Control chapter."
    }
  ]
}
